# ┌──────────┐
# │ ＩＮＦＯ │
# └──────────┘
# services talk to each other by service name
# this is why DATABASE_URL uses postgres and the 
# s3 uses rustfs
# leave those and adjust credentials/secrets
#
# ┌──────────────────────┐
# │ ＰＯＳＴＧＲＥＳＱＬ │
# └──────────────────────┘
# some data is a bit redundant but 
# set for docker compose
POSTGRES_USER=""
# openssl rand -base64 24
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=""
POSTGRES_DB=""
# host/port the db:* scripts connect to (run from the host, not the compose network)
POSTGRES_HOST="localhost"
POSTGRES_PORT="5432"
DATABASE_URL="postgres://appuser:change-me-long-random@postgres:5432/appdb"

# ┌──────────┐
# │ ＡＵＴＨ │
# └──────────┘
AUTH_SECRET=""                                     # openssl rand -base64 32
AUTH_DISCORD_ID=""
AUTH_DISCORD_SECRET=""

# notion secret stuff;
# this might be deleted in the future
NOTION_SECRET=""
NOTION_PRODUCTION_DB_ID=""
NOTION_NOTIFICITION_DB_ID=""

# production or dev
ENVIRONMENT="production"

# ┌──────┐
# │ Ｓ３ │
# └──────┘
S3_END_POINT="rustfs"
S3_PORT=9000
# openssl rand -hex 16
S3_ACCESS_KEY="" 
# openssl rand -hex 32
S3_SECRET_KEY=""
S3_BUCKET_NAME=""

# llm stuff
GEMINI_API=""

# ┌──────────────┐
# │ ＤＯＣＫＥＲ │
# └──────────────┘
DOCKER_REGISTRY=""
DOCKER_IMAGE_NAME=""
IMAGE_TAG=""

# must be "true" to allow the destructive db:dev:start / db:demo:start scripts
# and to seed demo data (see scripts/demo/lib/guard.ts)
DEMO_SEED=""

# must be "true" to render the helper bar (guides/links) at the bottom of the app
SHOW_HELPER_BAR=""
